{{!--
    ui/model-picker - the "which model" field of the AI page.

    A provider lists dozens of models, most of them unsuited to reading mail, and a <select> of
    bare names was a wall nobody could choose from. This is the account picker's shape over a list
    the page already holds: type any part of a name or an id, pick from the suggestions, and the
    box is replaced by a card naming the model, what it is for, and its id. Every entry carries a
    one-line note and the recommended ones are listed first, so the sane choice is also the easy
    one. The first entry is "Default", which follows the library's built-in model across upgrades.

    The list travels in the data-models attribute and can be replaced after a refresh with
    window.uiModelPickerSetModels(); the card is painted from the entry the value names. The
    markup is ui/picker.
      {{> ui/model-picker id="openAiModel" models=openAiModels value=values.openAiModel}}
    Params:
      id          - hidden input id, also the default posted name and what page scripts read (required)
      name        - posted field name (defaults to id)
      label       - field label (optional)
      hint        - muted helper text under the control (optional)
      error       - validation error message (optional)
      value       - current model name, empty for the default (optional)
      models      - the list: {id, name, description, recommended} entries, "Default" first (required)
      placeholder - search box placeholder (optional)
--}}
{{#if placeholder}}
{{> ui/picker kind="model" id=id name=name label=label hint=hint error=error value=value models=models placeholder=placeholder}}
{{else}}
{{> ui/picker kind="model" id=id name=name label=label hint=hint error=error value=value models=models placeholder="Search models by name or id"}}
{{/if}}
